 ## Overview
-Leaf Offset Computation computes the linear memory offsets for each leaf node within an OpenVDB tree to facilitate efficient parallel processing and data copying [S1, unofficial]. It serves as the final step in leaf collection, transforming a count of active leaves into a contiguous index array that maps leaf IDs to their starting positions in a flattened voxel buffer [S1, unofficial]. This method is distinct from [Leaf Node Representation](3000-leaf-node-representation.md), which defines the internal structure of individual leaves, by focusing on the global layout and indexing of the entire set of leaves rather than their local data organization.
